                                <h2 class="tr-animate">A POS that keeps selling offline</h2>
                                <p class="tr-animate tr-animate-delay-1">Odoo POS runs in the browser on a tablet, a PC or a touch terminal. After a session is opened, the till can continue to take orders if the internet connection drops, and the orders sync to the server once the connection returns. Queues at the counter do not depend on your network provider.</p>
                                <p class="tr-animate tr-animate-delay-1">Cashiers work with product search, barcode scanning, discounts, split payments and customer lookup. Managers open and close shifts, count cash and review a session report. Receipts and product names can be maintained in Arabic and English, and the interface supports right-to-left display.</p>
                            </div>
